codex
The first universal attempt exposed a proof-architecture issue: the big-step evaluator buried recursive calls inside functional terms, so K could not apply the reachability claim as a circularity. I’m switching the interpreter to a small-step continuation semantics. Recursive calls will then appear at the front of the `<k>` cell, which is the form K’s prover can use inductively.
apply patch
